Subject: System Settings: name the sidebar lists, frame and focus their current item, leave the sidebar by Shift+Tab from Search

The two sidebar lists, the categories and a category's pages, have the
list role and no name, so a screen reader entering one by Tab reads
"list" and nothing it can act on. The category list is named "Settings
categories", or "Search results" while a search is typed, and a
category's page list takes the category's title ("Colors & Themes").
Each list hands its focus scope's focus to its current item whenever the
list takes the active focus without it, so entering a list reads the
list's name and then its current item. Setting the item's focus, with no
Tab reason, leaves the style's own visual focus off.

Neither list shows where the keyboard focus is: the current item's
highlight looks the same with the focus anywhere else in the window. The
current item draws a frame in the theme's focus colour while its list
holds the active focus and the keyboard brought it there. A Tab into the
window hands the active focus to the list, which keeps that state, since
a focus scope stays active while its current item holds the focus. Every
focus entry into a list sets it, a Tab, Backtab, arrow key or a Right or
Enter that opens a category's pages alike, unless a pointer press on a
sidebar item caused the entry: a press marks the sidebar until the event
loop has run the click it ends in, and clears the frame of the list it
lands in. Losing the active focus clears it. A mouse click on an item
draws no frame, and Space keeps it.

The search field's Backtab goes to its KeyNavigation.left, which it does
not have, so a Shift+Tab from Search falls to the sidebar scene's own
focus chain and wraps to the category list, and the list's and the menu
button's backtabs close a loop of Show menu, Search and the list that
never returns to the page. The search field hands a Backtab to
systemsettings.focusPrevious(), as the page list's Back button does, so
Shift+Tab from a page reaches Show menu, Search and then the page's Help
button.

A section heading is a Kirigami.ListSectionHeader, an ItemDelegate, whose
default accessible name is its text with each '&' stripped as a mnemonic
marker: "Security & Privacy" is read "Security  Privacy". The heading
takes its section text as its accessible name.

---
diff --git a/app/qml/CategoriesPage.qml b/app/qml/CategoriesPage.qml
--- a/app/qml/CategoriesPage.qml
+++ b/app/qml/CategoriesPage.qml
@@ -58,8 +58,10 @@
 
                 KeyNavigation.down: categoryView
 
-                KeyNavigation.backtab: KeyNavigation.left
                 KeyNavigation.tab: KeyNavigation.right
+                Keys.onBacktabPressed: event => {
+                    systemsettings.focusPrevious();
+                }
 
                 Keys.onDownPressed: event => rowLayout.Keys.downPressed(event)
                 onActiveFocusChanged: {
@@ -123,6 +125,22 @@
         activeFocusOnTab: true
         keyNavigationWraps: true
         Accessible.role: Accessible.List
+        Accessible.name: mainColumn.searchMode
+            ? i18nc("@info:accessible", "Search results")
+            : i18nc("@info:accessible", "Settings categories")
+
+        // Whether the keyboard brought the focus to this list: set on every
+        // focus entry that no pointer press on a sidebar item caused, cleared
+        // by such a press and by the list losing the focus.
+        property bool keyboardFocus: false
+        onActiveFocusChanged: {
+            keyboardFocus = activeFocus && !root.itemPointerPress;
+            // Hand the scope's focus to the current item, so a screen reader
+            // entering the list reads that item after the list's name.
+            if (activeFocus && currentItem && !currentItem.activeFocus) {
+                currentItem.focus = true;
+            }
+        }
 
         KeyNavigation.up: searchField
         KeyNavigation.backtab: hamburgerMenuButton
@@ -144,6 +162,9 @@
 
                 width: ListView.view.width
                 label: section
+                // A button's default accessible name strips '&' as a mnemonic
+                // marker; the heading is read by its full text.
+                Accessible.name: section
             }
         }
 
@@ -174,6 +195,15 @@
             enabled: !isCategory || !mainColumn.searchMode
 
             highlighted: ListView.isCurrentItem
+            focusFrameVisible: ListView.isCurrentItem && categoryView.activeFocus && categoryView.keyboardFocus
+            onPointerActiveChanged: {
+                if (pointerActive) {
+                    root.itemPointerPress = true;
+                    categoryView.keyboardFocus = false;
+                } else {
+                    Qt.callLater(root.endItemPointerPress);
+                }
+            }
 
             onClicked: {
                 if (!enabled) { return; }
diff --git a/app/qml/CategoryItem.qml b/app/qml/CategoryItem.qml
--- a/app/qml/CategoryItem.qml
+++ b/app/qml/CategoryItem.qml
@@ -23,6 +23,33 @@
     Accessible.name: text
     Accessible.onPressAction: clicked()
 
+    // Set by the list that holds the item, the one that knows whether the
+    // keyboard brought its focus here.
+    property bool focusFrameVisible: false
+
+    // True while a pointer is pressed on the item. A Space key press makes
+    // the item pressed too, so the list reads this to tell a pointer from a
+    // key.
+    readonly property bool pointerActive: pointerPress.active
+
+    PointHandler {
+        id: pointerPress
+        acceptedButtons: Qt.AllButtons
+    }
+
+    Rectangle {
+        anchors.fill: parent
+        anchors.leftMargin: delegate.leftInset
+        anchors.rightMargin: delegate.rightInset
+        anchors.topMargin: delegate.topInset
+        anchors.bottomMargin: delegate.bottomInset
+        visible: delegate.focusFrameVisible
+        color: "transparent"
+        border.width: 1
+        border.color: Kirigami.Theme.focusColor
+        radius: Kirigami.Units.cornerRadius
+    }
+
     contentItem: RowLayout {
         spacing: Kirigami.Units.smallSpacing
 
diff --git a/app/qml/SideBarItem.qml b/app/qml/SideBarItem.qml
--- a/app/qml/SideBarItem.qml
+++ b/app/qml/SideBarItem.qml
@@ -21,6 +21,14 @@
     property alias searchMode: mainColumn.searchMode
     readonly property real headerHeight: mainColumn.header.height
 
+    // True from a pointer press on a sidebar item until the event loop has
+    // run the click it ends in, so the list a click hands the focus to
+    // draws no focus frame.
+    property bool itemPointerPress: false
+    function endItemPointerPress() {
+        itemPointerPress = false;
+    }
+
     CategoriesPage {
         id: mainColumn
         focus: true
